---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
// TODO OWNER: set the effective date below, and update this policy if you add analytics, a newsletter, ads or comments.
// This is a plain-language starting point, not legal advice.
const effective = 'November 21, 2026';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="How DriveTested handles information when you visit our site, including cookies set by Amazon when you click affiliate links."
>
  <p class="ui-small">Effective date: {effective}</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} doesn't require an account, doesn't sell personal information, and doesn't run third-party advertising
    trackers on this site. When you click a link to Amazon or another retailer, that retailer may set cookies so it can
    credit us for a sale.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider (Vercel) processes standard technical information such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested, to deliver the site and keep it secure.</li>
    <li><strong>Email you send us.</strong> If you contact us, we receive your email address and message and use them only to reply.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Affiliate links and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We participate in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program. When you click an Amazon link on our site, Amazon may
    place or read cookies in your browser to attribute purchases to us. Amazon's use of that information is covered by
    Amazon's own privacy notice. We don't receive your name, address or what you bought, only aggregated reports of
    qualifying purchases.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If we add privacy-friendly analytics to measure which pages are useful, we will update this policy to name the
    provider and what it collects.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Depending on where you live (for example in the EU, UK
    or California), you may have rights to access or delete personal information we hold about you. Contact us to
    make a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is intended for adults and is not directed to children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We'll update this page if our practices change and revise the effective date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
